From: uConsole Workbench contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: defer draining period notification until retirement

prepare_playback_urb advances hwptr_done while filling a not-yet-submitted
URB. At the final period boundary, notifying PCM core in DRAINING state can
stop the endpoint. The endpoint checks its running state after preparation
and then discards that final URB. Keep the notification pending until a
retirement callback, after the newly prepared URB has been submitted. The
existing keep_pending stop path can then finish the in-flight transfers.

Candidate for the pinned 6.12.62 source; requires guest and hardware testing.

--- a/sound/usb/pcm.c
+++ b/sound/usb/pcm.c
@@ -1578,7 +1578,9 @@ static int prepare_playback_urb(struct snd_usb_substream *subs,
 		subs->trigger_tstamp_pending_update = false;
 	}
 
-	if (period_elapsed && !subs->running && subs->lowlatency_playback) {
+	if (period_elapsed &&
+	    ((!subs->running && subs->lowlatency_playback) ||
+	     runtime->state == SNDRV_PCM_STATE_DRAINING)) {
 		subs->period_elapsed_pending = 1;
 		period_elapsed = 0;
 	}
